WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.467
-They love you!
-Aw, I love you, guys.

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:03.968
-We love you. Welcome to the --

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:05.901
I want to say
welcome back to the show

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:08.200
because you actually made
your late-night debut

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:09.968
on our show
with "Drivers License."

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:11.901
-"Drivers License." Yep.
-But we never chatted.

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:13.367
-I know.
I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:14.801
I'm such a fan of the show.

00:00:14.801 --> 00:00:17.200
Growing up, I used to watch it
every night with my parents.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.400
I'm such a huge fan,
so it's an honor to be here.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.434
You actually -- I met you,
um, maybe three year--

00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:24.501
You wouldn't have remembered.
It was -- It was so long ago.

00:00:24.501 --> 00:00:25.968
-What do you mean,
I wouldn't remember?

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:27.734
-It was in a group of people,
but there was a group of people,

00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:29.167
and they were like,
"Hey, hey, hey."

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:31.400
And you actually went up to
my mom and you gave her a hug.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.901
And it is her bragging rights
for the rest of her life.

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:35.501
She loves you so much.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:37.968
-She sends her regards and she
says, "Thank you for the hug."

00:00:37.968 --> 00:00:41.501
-Hi, Mom! Hi! Yeah.

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:44.067
Uh, I follow you
on the socials, and I --

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:46.300
You're a great fellow,
by the way,

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.868
if you like the social media.

00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:51.133
But I noticed that
you don't follow anyone back.

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:52.701
-Oh. I'm sorry.

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:55.000
If I was following one person,
it'd be you, though, I hope.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.400
-Thank you. Oh, yeah.
Really, though...

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.400
-Ah, [bleep].
-Any reason why?

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:03.334
-No, you know,
I try to follow zero people

00:01:03.334 --> 00:01:05.367
because it helps me
be off of my phone,

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:07.000
you know,
off of social media.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.601
But I had this very embarrassing
encounter once

00:01:10.601 --> 00:01:13.267
where I was stalking my ex,
as one does.

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:15.167
Sue me. Sorry.

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:18.000
And, um --
And I accidentally followed him

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.667
because I was stalking him, and
I was just following one person,

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:22.434
so it was super obvious
that I was following him.

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:24.968
And my friend ran into my room
and was like, "Oh, my God!

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:26.801
Did you mean to follow him?
Like, unfollow him!"

00:01:26.801 --> 00:01:28.200
And I went
and I grabbed my phone.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.567
I'm like,
"Oh, shoot! Oh, my God!"

00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:31.067
And I went to open
the Instagram app.

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:33.400
And the second that I opened
the app, my phone died.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.100
-Oh, my gosh!
-Couldn't find the charger.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.934
So I was just following
my ex for a while.

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:39.634
-Did it come out
that you were --

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:42.334
Yeah, and people were like,
"Oh, my gosh! She's hacked!"

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:45.234
And I'm like, "Yeah, you guys.
Be safe." Like...

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:47.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:49.200
"Get your two-factor
authentication, you guys."

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.934
-You weren't hacked it all.
You did it yourself.

00:01:50.934 --> 00:01:52.634
-Yeah. Sorry.
-Oh, my gosh. Alright.

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.834
So now -- But you don't make
that mistake again.

00:01:54.834 --> 00:01:56.567
-No, no. I have a Finsta now,
so I'm safe.

00:01:56.567 --> 00:01:58.167
-You have a finsta.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:58.167 --> 00:02:00.267
Do you have a Finsta, Jimmy.
-I need a Finsta.

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:02.200
-Yeah. You need a Finsta.
-A fake Instagram.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:03.601
-Fake Instagram. Yeah.

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:05.133
So you can just lurk
and be curious.

00:02:05.133 --> 00:02:07.033
-Yeah. And like things
and look at things and...

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:08.868
Wait. I'm totally getting
a Finsta this week.

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:09.901
-Yeah. Okay.
-Alright. Thank you.

00:02:09.901 --> 00:02:11.334
I appreciate it.
I want to talk to you.

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:12.934
I have so many things
to talk to you about.

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:15.033
First of all,
congratulations on "GUTS."

00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:16.868
-Thank you.
-Uh, this is unbelievable.

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:18.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:18.334 --> 00:02:21.434
Went right to number one
when it released.

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:23.934
And then you got nominated
just now for six Grammys.

00:02:23.934 --> 00:02:25.634
Uh...

00:02:25.634 --> 00:02:27.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:31.234
You have three Grammys on your
shelf already from "Sour,"

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:33.133
but how does it feel
to be nominated for six?

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:35.200
I mean, you're part of this --
This is your year now.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.267
-It's so surreal.
I actually can't believe it.

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:38.934
I feel like
the luckiest girl alive.

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:40.968
I used to go
to the Grammy Museum

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:42.968
all the time when I was younger,
and, actually,

00:02:42.968 --> 00:02:45.300
my mom and I used to, like,
make ballots for the Grammys,

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.534
like, when the Grammys
were on TV.

00:02:46.534 --> 00:02:47.667
When I was like 12, I'd be like,

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.267
"I think this album
is going to win."

00:02:49.267 --> 00:02:51.033
And, like, we'd do --
place bets and stuff.

00:02:51.033 --> 00:02:52.567
-No way!
-So it's a super-big deal.

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:53.801
Yeah, it's just --
it's such an honor

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:55.133
to be included in a group

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:57.901
with all these artists
that I just am so inspired by.

00:02:57.901 --> 00:02:59.634
-You more than
hold your own, bud.

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:02.033
And now here we go.
This "Hunger Games" soundtrack.

00:03:02.033 --> 00:03:05.501
The new song is called
"Can't Catch Me Now."

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:08.968
What's it like writing a song
for a movie or, like --

00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:10.133
Because you're not --

00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:11.934
This, you write
your songs for you.

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:13.367
-Yeah, that's like my diary,

00:03:13.367 --> 00:03:15.767
but this was a totally
different experience for me

00:03:15.767 --> 00:03:17.200
as a songwriter.
It was so much fun.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:19.968
I'm such a big fan
of all things "Hunger Games,"

00:03:19.968 --> 00:03:22.767
and I love the soundtracks,
and so when they asked

00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:24.367
if I wanted to write it,
I was so stoked.

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:26.501
And I went in
and watched the movie

00:03:26.501 --> 00:03:29.033
and was really inspired by
the main character, Lucy Gray.

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:31.234
Um, and so it was super-fun
to get to write a song

00:03:31.234 --> 00:03:33.534
through her eyes.
It was definitely a big stretch

00:03:33.534 --> 00:03:35.567
for me as a songwriter.
It was really fun.

00:03:35.567 --> 00:03:37.167
-Well, February is gonna
be a giant month for you

00:03:37.167 --> 00:03:39.434
because you have the Grammys,

00:03:39.434 --> 00:03:41.167
you turn 21, by the way.
-Yeah.

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:43.400
-Happy birthday.
Happy early birthday.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.567
-I'm very excited
about that one.

00:03:46.567 --> 00:03:48.334
-And you're kicking off
your "GUTS" world tour.

00:03:48.334 --> 00:03:49.801
This is what everyone's
talking about

00:03:49.801 --> 00:03:52.300
and trying to get tickets for.
I mean, this is wild.

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:54.133
You're gonna play
all these giant arenas.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.634
-Yeah.
-Do you get nervous

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:57.000
when you do these giant gigs?

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.234
-Oh, man. So nervous.
I get super nervous. Yeah.

00:04:00.234 --> 00:04:03.334
I saw you at the Jingle Ball
last week, and I was like --

00:04:03.334 --> 00:04:05.901
And you were so kind of calm...
-Yeah.

00:04:05.901 --> 00:04:09.267
-...to be performing for,
you know, 20,000, 30,000 people.

00:04:09.267 --> 00:04:11.067
-Yeah, you know, it's different.

00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:13.100
I feel like playing
your own show is a lot more fun

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:14.968
because there's just so many
people in the audience,

00:04:14.968 --> 00:04:16.467
and sometimes they know
the lyrics, too,

00:04:16.467 --> 00:04:18.100
so if you, like, forget a lyric,
you're like,

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.834
"Throw it to the crowd!"
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:19.834 --> 00:04:21.834
Is there a song you're psyched
to play live?

00:04:21.834 --> 00:04:24.067
-Ooh, um, I'm really excited.

00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:26.133
I wrote this song called
"All-American Bitch"

00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:27.868
that I really like.
-Yeah. I love that one.

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:30.100
-Yeah, so,
it's super-fun and rowdy,

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.167
and I just hope people
can, like,

00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:33.701
scream and dance and go crazy.

00:04:33.701 --> 00:04:35.834
-Yeah!
Guys, get prepared to sing.

00:04:35.834 --> 00:04:37.267
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:37.267 --> 00:04:39.567
Uh, we found something online

00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:41.601
that I wanted
to ask you about.

00:04:41.601 --> 00:04:43.267
There's a -- There's a thing
that said that you once

00:04:43.267 --> 00:04:46.467
wrote an original Christmas song
when you were 5.

00:04:46.467 --> 00:04:48.501
-Yeah. Yeah.
-Do you remember doing this?

00:04:48.501 --> 00:04:51.000
-Start 'em young. I don't even
remember. No, I don't.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.434
But, yeah, I know
what you're talking about.

00:04:52.434 --> 00:04:54.467
-It was called "The Bels"
or something like that.

00:04:54.467 --> 00:04:58.467
The album cover's online.
-Oh! Look at that.

00:04:58.467 --> 00:05:00.367
-Yeah.
-B-E-L-S.

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:02.734
-Close. Very close.
-Yeah.

00:05:02.734 --> 00:05:04.968
You know, I couldn't write,
but it didn't stop me

00:05:04.968 --> 00:05:06.534
from writing a song.
-Yeah. No.

00:05:06.534 --> 00:05:08.467
I like the "Bels" with one L.
Why not?

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:09.901
-Yeah.
-What was it about?

00:05:09.901 --> 00:05:12.033
Do you remember the song at all?
What was it about?

00:05:12.033 --> 00:05:14.367
-Oh, I think it's like, um --

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:16.033
I think it's about, like,
waiting for Santa,

00:05:16.033 --> 00:05:18.200
like, waiting to hear,
like, bells or something.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.100
-Five years old.
-Yeah.

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:21.868
-I wish we had it, but --
Actually we do.

00:05:21.868 --> 00:05:23.567
-Oh.

00:05:23.567 --> 00:05:26.000
-We found a copy of it.
And thanks, Mom.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:28.000
Here's the original song,
"The Bels,"

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.434
a snippet from
5-year-old Olivia Rodriguez.

00:05:30.434 --> 00:05:31.868
-Man, man.

00:05:31.868 --> 00:05:33.334
-♪ Ho, ho, ho, ho ♪

00:05:33.334 --> 00:05:34.834
♪ Wait for the bells ♪

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.167
[ Laughs ]

00:05:36.167 --> 00:05:37.467
♪ When you hear them ♪

00:05:37.467 --> 00:05:40.267
♪ Put the ornaments
on the tree ♪

00:05:40.267 --> 00:05:42.701
♪ Ho, ho, ho, ho ♪

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:45.300
♪ Wait for the bells ♪

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:48.667
♪ Wait for the bells
on Santa's sleigh to ring ♪

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:50.267
♪ Ho, ho, ho, ho ♪

00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:53.133
-Oh!
♪ Ho, ho, ho, ho, ho ♪

00:05:53.133 --> 00:05:54.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:56.367
I like that. That's a jam.
-Man.

00:05:56.367 --> 00:05:58.300
-You wrote a jam at 5 years old.

00:05:58.300 --> 00:05:59.901
-Thanks. Sheesh. Wow.

00:05:59.901 --> 00:06:03.400
-Olivia, you kind of, like,
manifested this career, which...

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:04.901
-I suppose so.

00:06:04.901 --> 00:06:07.767
I mean, I was writing songs,
like, at such an early age.

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:10.067
Yeah, I've always been into it.
-And you had a pop --

00:06:10.067 --> 00:06:12.400
a pop-star themed birthday party
when you were 6.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:13.834
-Yes. I did, I did.

00:06:13.834 --> 00:06:15.467
-And your mom also
gave us a photo of this.

00:06:15.467 --> 00:06:16.934
-Oh, wow.
Walk down memory lane today.

00:06:16.934 --> 00:06:18.667
-She's the b--
I'm glad I hugged her that day.

00:06:18.667 --> 00:06:21.100
She's totally writing
this whole interview for me.

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:22.767
This is you
on your 6th birthday,

00:06:22.767 --> 00:06:24.167
a pop-star themed party.
-Oh, man!

00:06:24.167 --> 00:06:26.968
-And you even had, like,
a play-- like, a set list.

00:06:26.968 --> 00:06:29.200
-Yeah. Wow. Yeah.
I really manifested this hard.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:31.567
Yeah. There was not an audience.
No one was watching.

00:06:31.567 --> 00:06:33.968
But I just had all of my,
like, kindergarten friends,

00:06:33.968 --> 00:06:35.667
and we were just singing,
like, the Jonas Brothers.

00:06:35.667 --> 00:06:37.567
We were really into it.
-Isn't that fantastic?

00:06:37.567 --> 00:06:39.000
-Yeah.
-And now this weekend,

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.667
you're going to be musical
guest on "Saturday Night Live."

00:06:40.667 --> 00:06:42.734
-Ahh!
-I mean, look at you, bud.

00:06:42.734 --> 00:06:45.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:06:45.667 --> 00:06:48.033
-I think the last time
you actually did perform

00:06:48.033 --> 00:06:50.334
"Saturday Night Live," right?
-Yeah, I did.

00:06:50.334 --> 00:06:52.901
It was actually
my second time performing ever,

00:06:52.901 --> 00:06:54.367
like, my own songs
in front of --

00:06:54.367 --> 00:06:56.133
Besides that.
I mean, that doesn't count.

00:06:56.133 --> 00:06:57.834
-Yeah. No. Yeah.
"The Bels." Of course.

00:06:57.834 --> 00:06:58.868
-"The Bels." Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:58.868 --> 00:07:00.400
Um, but, yeah,
I'm really excited.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.701
The first time I ever did it --
-Do you like the pressure?

00:07:02.701 --> 00:07:04.267
I mean, do you like to go in
like, "Yeah, go ahead,

00:07:04.267 --> 00:07:06.234
I'll do the Super Bowl,
give it to me, let's go"?

00:07:06.234 --> 00:07:07.934
It's like, "Why not?"
And just go for it.

00:07:07.934 --> 00:07:09.634
-I get really nervous.
-You do?

00:07:09.634 --> 00:07:11.467
-It's just -- It's live-live.
I mean, you know.

00:07:11.467 --> 00:07:13.567
Do you have any tips for me?
You're a --

00:07:13.567 --> 00:07:15.033
-No. Just enjoy it.
-Yeah?

00:07:15.033 --> 00:07:17.234
-Yeah. That's it.
I love doing live.

00:07:17.234 --> 00:07:18.901
I love a live audience.
Nothing like it.

00:07:18.901 --> 00:07:21.300
I mean, it's the best.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:23.534
They tell you --
You feed off the energy.

00:07:23.534 --> 00:07:25.167
-Yeah.
-You're going to crush it.

00:07:25.167 --> 00:07:27.400
I can't wait to watch.
Olivia Rodrigo, everybody.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.801
"Can't Catch Me Now" is out now.

00:07:29.801 --> 00:07:32.200
Olivia and I are doing
something fun after the break.

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:35.467
Stick around. Come on back.
More with Olivia Rodrigo.

